\begin_body

\begin_layout Title
Parallel Pipeline for Genomic Selection
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Introduction
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The ppGS library was developed for easy and parallel computation of a pipeline
 for genomic selection (GS) on potato color traits from AGROSAVIA's Colombian
 Central Collection (CCC).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Installation
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The package 
\series bold
ppGS
\series default
 is sitting on GitHub repo: 
\begin_inset Flex URL
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

https://github.com/luisgarreta/ppGS
\end_layout

\end_inset

.
 To install it, first, you need to install the 
\series bold
devtools
\series default
 package.
 You can do this from CRAN.
 Invoke R and then type:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset listings
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

install.packages("devtools")
\end_layout

\end_inset

 Load the devtools package.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset listings
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

library(devtools) 
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In most cases, you just use install_github("author/package").
 For the package 
\series bold
ppGS
\series default
, you’d type:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset listings
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

install_github("luisgarreta/ppGS")
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Genotypic data
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The CCC genotypic data includes two tables: a genotype matrix and a color
 phenotype table.
 The library has a utility function called 
\series bold
gs_datasets
\series default
 that creates different datasets.
 For example, to get a copy of the original genotype/phenotype, call the
 function as follows.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset listings
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

gs_datasets (type="sources")
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This function extracts the genotypic data (genotype and phenotype), creates
 a "sources" directory and copies them as files into it.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Genotype structure 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The genotype consists of a table with markers in the rows, observations
 in the columns and tetraploid genotype values in each cell.
 The following is an excerpt from this file:
\begin_inset listings
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

geno = read.csv ("sources/sources-genotypes-CCC-Andigena-ClusterCall2020.csv",
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

                  check.names=F) 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

geno [1:5, 1:8]
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

Markers 15060006 15060013 15060016 15060021 15060025 15060027 15060039
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

c1_1        4        4        4        4        4        4        3
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

c1_1000     2        1        2        2        2        2        1
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

c1_10000    1        0        1        1        0        0        1
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

c1_10001    3        4        3        3        4        4        3
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

c1_10011    1        0        1        1        0        0        2
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The original marker names were simplified from "solcap_snp_XXX" to "XXX"
 (e.g., "solcap_snp_c1_1" has been changed to "c1_1").
 And the names of the observations were changed to their record number,
 as opposed to their old access identifier (e.g., "And_10" has been changed
 to "15060006").
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Phenotype structure 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The phenotype data consists of a table with the observations in the rows,
 the color phenotypes in the columns, and the phenotype values in each cell.
 An excerpt from this file is shown below:
\begin_inset listings
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

phenos= read.csv ("sources/sources-phenotypes-CCC-Andigena-ColorTraitsHCL.csv",
  
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

                   check.names=F) 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

phenos [1:5, 1:6]
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

Samples Tallo.LCH.L Tallo.LCH.C Tallo.LCH.H PriFlor.LCH.L PriFlor.LCH.C 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

15060006     28          16         359            52            45 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

15060013     NA          NA          NA            54            49 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

15061904     28          16         359            36            55 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

15060016     28          16         359            45            57 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

15060021     28          16         359            37            43
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Each row corresponds to an observation and each column to a color phenotype,
 in total there are 24 phenotypes corresponding to eight color characteristics
 measured in potato and decomposed into three components of the HCL color
 space with "H" for huge, "C" for chroma and "L" for luminance.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The eight characteristics are "PriFlower" for flower primary color, "Baya"
 for berry color, "PriTuber" for tuber primary color, "SecTuber" for tuber
 secondary color, "Pulpa" for flesh color, "PriBrote" for bud primary color,
 and "SecBrote" for bud secondary color.
\end_layout

