\begin_layout Subsection
Training/testing datasets
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The parameters for running GS with the 
\series bold
gs_multi
\series default
 function need training and target datasets for genotype and phenotype.
 Just to test this function, you can generate these datasets using the 
\series bold
gs_datasets
\series default
 function in this way:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset listings
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

gs_datasets (type=
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

small
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

>>> Copying small datasets to /home/lg/agrosavia/COLOR-TRAITS/GS-PKG/ppGS/vignet
tes
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

small-config.yml         
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

small-target-geno.csv
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

small-target-pheno.csv
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

small-training-geno.csv
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

small-training-pheno.csv
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The above call using type="small" generates a small dataset containing 1000
 markers and 6 phenotypes.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In contrast, you can generate a complete dataset containing 4640 markers
 and 24 traits in this way:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset listings
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

gs_datasets (type=
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

full
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

)
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Running GS
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Running GS can take a few minutes or several minutes depending on your machine,
 the number of cores used in parallel, and the type of data sets.
 The small dataset may take a few minutes (1 to 3 minutes, with 4 cores),
 but the full dataset may take several minutes (8 to 10 minutes, with 4
 cores).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To run GS with the small datasets, execute:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset listings
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

gs_datasets (type=
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

small
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

setwd (
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

small
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

gs_multi (configFile=
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

small-config.yml
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

, outputDir=
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

smallGS
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

)
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Now, to run GS with the full datasets, execute:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset listings
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

gs_datasets (type=
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

full
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

setwd (
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

full
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

gs_multi (configFile=
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

full-config.yml
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

, outputDir=
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

fullGS
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

)
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Results 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The 
\series bold
gs_multi
\series default
 function generates two types of results: first, a table with the GEBVs
 for each phenotype, and second, boxplots comparing the predictions of the
 phenotypes.
 In both outputs, the values are calculated with the best prediction method
 for each phenotype, i.e., the methods with maximum predictive ability (PA),
 where PA is measured by the correlation between the actual phenotype and
 the GEBV of the cross-validation.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
GEBVs for each phenotype
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
GEBVs are given for each observation (rows) and each phenotype (columns).
 If the target phenotype file with actual values was specified in the configurat
ion file, these values are shown next to the GEVBs.
 An excerpt of this table is shown below:
