\begin_layout Subsubsection
Best prediction methods for phenotypes
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This result is provided in two ways: a graphical comparison of the PA for
 each phenotype calculated for the best method, and a table with the PA
 results from cross-validation.
 The figure below shows the GS results using complete datasets.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Float figure
placement H
wide false
sideways false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\align center
\begin_inset Graphics
	filename images/out-CrossValidation-ModelsTraits-FULL.pdf
	lyxscale 50
	scale 40

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset Caption Standard

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Best prediction methods using full markers.
 
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Results of GS using selected markers
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The configuration file for GS contains two optional parameters called "markersFi
le" and "nMarkers", the first for a file name of a table with selected marker
 names (e.g.
 best markers resulting from a GWAS analysis) and the second for the number
 of markers to take from this table.
 If these parameters are present (not NULL), the 
\series bold
gs_multi
\series default
 function takes only these markers to execute the whole GS process.
 The following figure shows the results of a GS using the results of a previous
 GWAS analysis and selecting from it the best 50 markers:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Float figure
placement H
wide false
sideways false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\align center
\begin_inset Graphics
	filename images/out-CrossValidation-ModelsTraits-GWAS50.pdf
	lyxscale 50
	scale 40

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset Caption Standard

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Comparison of prediction methods using 50 selected markers from GWAS.
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To compare the above results using selected GWAS markers, the following
 figure shows the results of GS using 50 random markers from the full set
 of markers:
\end_layout

