\begin_layout Subsection
Running GS 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To test the GS run with a single phenotype, you can use the 
\series bold
gs_datasets
\series default
 function to create training/target genotypes/phenotypes with their respective
 configuration, change to the directory with the datasets and run 
\series bold
gs_single
\series default
 as follows:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset listings
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

gs_datasets (type=
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

single
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

setwd (
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

single
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

gs_single (configFile=
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

single-config.yml
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

, outputDir=
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

singleGS
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

)
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Results of GS
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The
\series bold
 gs_single
\series default
 function generates several outputs (Figure 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "fig:Outputs-from-GS"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"

\end_inset

): (a) Table of GEBVs along with the actual value (if the target phenotype
 file was specified in the configuration file); (b) Histogram and correlation
 between GEBVs and training values; (c) Histogram and correlation between
 GEBVs and the actual values of the phenotypes (if the target phenotype
 file was specified in the configuration file); (d) Comparison of predictive
 ability by methods; (e) Run time of the methods; and (f) Correlations between
 the results of the different methods.
\end_layout

