\begin_layout Section
Heritability
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The heritability for multiple phenotypes can be calculated with the 
\series bold
gs_heritability
\series default
 function that takes three parameters: genotype matrix filename, phenotype
 table filename, and output directory name.
 For example, to calculate the heritabilities of the source genotype and
 phenotype, call the function as follows:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset listings
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

# Get copies of source genotype matrix and phenotypes table
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

gs_datasets (type=
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

sources
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

# Change to 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

sources
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 directory
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

setwd (
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

sources
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

# Calculate heritabilities
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

gs_heritability (
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

sources-genotypes-CCC-Andigena-ClusterCall2020.csv
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

,
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

                 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

sources-phenotypes-CCC-Andigena-ColorTraitsHCL.csv
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

,
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

                 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

outputs
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

)
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Create the "outputs" directory and save in it two files: a table (CSV) with
 several heritabilities for each phenotype and a summary plot (PDF) comparing
 the average heritabilities of each phenotype.
 The summary plot is shown in the figure below:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Float figure
